# mug_table_100 at a 250 ms round trip: the host plays each mug's flight further behind its
# thrower, and still shows every table pushed no farther than the same throw pushes it solo.
scenario mug_table_250
scene mug_tables
seed 41
guests 1
settle 6s

net g1 rtt 250ms jitter 10ms loss 1%

p1 grab mug_a as lift_a
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 3.05 0.1 -2.4 speed 7 as throw_a
p1 wait 1s
p1 grab mug_b as lift_b
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 3.05 0.4 0 speed 9 as throw_b
p1 wait 1s
p1 grab mug_c as lift_c
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 3.05 0.1 2 speed 11 as throw_c

expect result lift_a granted
expect result lift_b granted
expect result lift_c granted
expect result throw_c done
# Derived margin, 0.36 cm. A table leaves a hit at m v / (m + M) at most (0.3 kg mug, 6 kg table)
# and friction (sqrt(0.6 x 0.3), g 12) stops it over u^2 / (2 mu g): at most 1.1 cm at 7 m/s and
# 2.7 cm at 11 m/s, growing with the square of the hit's speed.
# HOST: the host simulates the table, struck by its dynamic copy of the mug, which the seam drives
# near the host's bodies no faster than the thrower's mug as played (1/32 m/s a component: 0.027
# m/s off): the correction steers a flight there and never speeds it, so neither playback
# catching up its clock nor a path rejoined after lost states hits harder. A copy played past the guest's last state goes on its own
# motion, and the host takes the flight back from the copy, not from that state. 0.027 m/s is 0.8 %
# of the slide at 7 m/s and 0.5 % at 11 m/s: 0.2 mm.
# INTERACTION: the thrower takes the table (under the 20 kg light mass) at the hit and simulates
# it with her own mug, solo's physics less what her copy kept of the hit in that step; the host's
# dynamic copy follows her and is left as its world settled it within SYNC_SOFT_HOLD_M of her rest
# pose: 3.4 mm.
expect moved table_a <= solo 0.36cm
expect moved table_b <= solo 0.36cm
expect moved table_c <= solo 0.36cm
# Every mug hit its table: a travel past the rest hold's 3.4 mm is no rounding of a pose at rest.
# (Under heavy loss a refused take can miss one: a missed effect, README "Contact claims".)
expect moved table_a >= 0.34cm
expect moved table_b >= 0.34cm
expect moved table_c >= 0.34cm
expect agree_at_rest 5cm 5deg
expect no_stuck
